summary: A sum of squared affine rows of any number, a linear term and a constant, in the tangent coordinates of several points at fixed anchors, is Gaussian along its rows and flat or linear across them; such factors add, are a normal exactly when their rows have full rank, and are what integrating a variable out of a linear-Gaussian model leaves on its neighbours, the Kalman filter's update and prediction among them.
